{
  "Motif": "magic-users",
  "Name": "Magic-users",
  "Draw": "Magic users are ordinary human bodies doing extraordinary things with their hands. Heavy layered robes, hoods, stoles, and belts hung with tools and tokens; staves, rods, open books, chalk and written work. The physique says nothing - the read is the face, the hands, and what the hands are making. The element belongs to the spell rather than to the caster, so it lives in the light coming off the hands and the staff, and that light is what illuminates the face.",
  "ElementDraw": {
    "fire": "The spell is orange. Flame standing clear of the palms and the staff head, sparks lifting, the robe hems edged hot, and every shadow on the face thrown upward by what is being cast.",
    "ice": "The spell is pale blue. Frost spreading from the fingertips back across the sleeve, a fog of cold pouring off the open hand, rime climbing the staff.",
    "lightning": "The spell is yellow. Arcs standing between the fingers and jumping to the staff, hair and robe hems lifted, the flicker sharp and blue-white at its core.",
    "earth": "The spell is green. Rough stone and crystal growing up the forearms and out of the staff head, dust hanging in the air, the robes dragged heavy by the weight of it.",
    "arcane": "The spell is violet. Script and sigils burning in the air around the hands, light leaking from the eyes and the mouth, and the edges of the robe not quite finished settling."
  },
  "ValidFloors": [
    4,
    8
  ],
